# Line-ending policy.
#
# Part of this tree was originally written from a Windows editor and landed with
# CRLF endings, while newer files use LF. The mix is invisible day to day but
# makes `gofmt -l` flag whole files as unformatted (it rewrites every line), so
# CI cannot check formatting until the tree is consistent.
#
# Normalize every text file to LF, both in the repository and in working trees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts and Dockerfiles are executed by Linux tooling — LF is required,
# not merely preferred.
*.sh   text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary assets: never inspected for line endings, never converted.
*.png binary
